== method ==
Question: how do the reading and the task grow as the scope takes in more rooms, from Part I's real start?

Start: results/start-part1.jsonl, seed 1 (frame 2728, room 33, 3,653 facts). The same map is the start and the
input of domains.build(start, goals). Goal: results/end-part1.json goal_all: owner:901, owner:902 and owner:903 = 1
(the ego). The planner is not run.

Room graph, from the IR alone (no route data). Room R links to room R' when code that belongs to R has a room
change with a constant target R'. Code that belongs to R: R's entry and exit code, R's local scripts, and the
scripts of the objects whose room (index.json) is R. Room changes: loadRoom(R') and loadRoomWithEgo(obj, R'). A
pseudo room (>= 0x80) is mapped to its room resource (model.Game.pseudo; 45 room changes). A change to R itself is
not a link (44 room changes). Not links: Resource.loadRoom (a resource load), actorFollowCamera and putActorInRoom
(no constant room). Global scripts are not part of the graph.
Result: 109 room changes are links: 100 distinct links, out of 53 of the 83 rooms. From room 33, 26 rooms are
reachable, in rings of 1, 3, 6, 12 and 4 rooms at distance 0 to 4. The other 57 rooms are reached only through
global scripts (the map, the ship, cutscenes) or through rooms with no constant room change.

Scope k: the rooms within k links of room 33. reader.Scope.of adds the global scripts they reach.
