155 of the game's 178 global scripts are reachable from the 83 rooms. "Goal writable" is Scope.writes.has. At k=1
it holds only through a wildcard: a write to 'owner:' whose object does not fold. The exact writes of owner:901,
902 and 903 (pickupObject(901..903)) are in room 83's local script 200 (the dock), which enters at k=2.

Measurement script: size_scaling.py (new). Per scope, one child process: Game.load, domains.build, Scope.of,
Reader, Builder, read_all(workers=16), build_task, relevance.relevant, reader.prune, task.write_sas of the pruned
task and its file written to the VM's disk (head, state, tail), then write_sas of the task before relevance and its
file. Each file is deleted after its size is taken. A supervisor process samples memory every 2 s. It kills the
scope when the machine's memory in use (MemTotal - MemAvailable) passes 100 GB, or when a step passes 60 minutes.
The line then names the step. Growth stops at the first scope that hits a limit. For k=2, a shell loop also
sampled /proc/stat every 30 s, for the machine's CPU seconds (the child is killed before it can report its own).

What ran:
- Local test: scope 0 on the laptop (8 CPUs, 23.2 GB, workers=4, 3 GB free-memory floor), same sources as the VM:
  878 records, 816 actions, 3,123 operators before relevance, 14.0 s wall, lowest free memory 3.77 GB.
- VM: Google Cloud n2-highmem-16 Spot (16 vCPUs, 125.8 GB), workers=16, --full-sas. k=0 and k=1 ran in one
  launch (17:22 to 17:52 UTC on 2026-10-24), k=2 in a second launch (17:55 UTC). All three scopes ran on the same
  uploaded sources: reader.py 94d495853f07 and model.py cc630446bdbe (sha1, 12 hex; the full list is above).
- A first attempt of this job (2026-10-23 23:32 UTC, model.py e413983eaf2d, same reader.py) ran k=0 and k=1 to
  the end and stopped k=2 at the 60-minute read limit. Its counts match this run's for k=0 and k=1 (878 and
  237,262 records) and for k=2's first two stages (163,981 and 229,680 records).

