columns: rooms, global scripts and units in the scope (reader.Scope.of); records: paths read (read_all, last pass); actions and effects: build_task; kept: actions relevance keeps; ops: operators in the task file after relevance and prune; ops full, MB full: the task file of the task before relevance; read s, read CPU s: read_all's wall and CPU (parent and workers); build s: build_task; relev s: relevance; parent GB: the scope process's peak RSS over its steps (VmHWM); worker GB: the largest pool worker's peak RSS (RUSAGE_CHILDREN); mem GB: the machine's memory in use at its peak minus before the scope (MemTotal - MemAvailable, sampled every 2 s; the 100 GB limit applies to this measure). For a scope stopped in the read step, read s is the time until the stop, read CPU s the whole machine's CPU seconds from /proc/stat over that time, and parent GB and worker GB are the supervisor's samples every 2 s.

